INVITATION TO TENDER

ANNUAL GROUNDS MAINTENANCE SERVICES

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Client:           Dame Hannah Rogers Trust
                  Woodland Road, Ivybridge

Contract Period:  1st March 2026 – 28th February 2027
                  (52 weeks)

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1. INTRODUCTION

Dame Hannah Rogers Trust invites suitably qualified contractors
to submit a quotation for the provision of annual grounds
maintenance services at Woodland Road, Ivybridge. This document
sets out the full specification of works required.

Tenderers are invited to submit their proposed pricing against
the scope of works and hours detailed below.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

2. SCOPE OF WORKS

The following maintenance activities are required throughout the
contract period:

  2.1  Hedge Cutting
       Cutting and trimming of all boundary hedges and internal
       hedges/shrubs as required to maintain a neat and tidy
       appearance, including the removal of all arisings.

  2.2  Grass Cutting
       Regular cutting of all lawned areas within the grounds
       and external verges to a maintained height appropriate
       to the season, including edging of borders and paths.

  2.3  Arthur's Area Maintenance
       Dedicated maintenance of Arthur's area, including
       general upkeep and presentation of the space.

  2.4  Weed Treatment
       Application of approved weed killer to all hard
       surfaces, including patios, paths and driveways within
       the grounds, as required throughout the season.

  2.5  Leaf Clearance
       Leaf blowing and collection across all areas of the
       grounds as required, particularly during the autumn
       period, to keep the site clean and safe.

  2.6  General Grounds Maintenance
       Any surplus time within the contracted hours will be
       utilised to carry out general maintenance works as
       directed by the client, ensuring the grounds remain in
       good order throughout the year.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

3. STAFFING & HOURS

  Operatives:      1 x Qualified Groundsman (minimum)
  Hours per week:  16 hours
  Contract weeks:  52 weeks per year
  Total hours:     832 hours per annum

Tenderers should confirm the number and qualifications of
operatives proposed to fulfil this contract.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

4. INCLUSIONS & EXCLUSIONS

  Required inclusions in the tender price:
    - Public liability insurance (copy to be provided on award)
    - Use of all contractor's own machinery and equipment
    - All routine labour as detailed in the scope of works above

  Excluded from the contract (not required):
    - Waste removal and disposal
    - Fuel costs (to be borne by the contractor)
    - Materials (e.g. herbicides, fertilisers) — to be priced
      separately if required

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

5. TENDER REQUIREMENTS

Tenderers are asked to provide the following with their
submission:

  - Total annual price (exclusive and inclusive of VAT)
  - Proposed payment schedule
  - Confirmation of public liability insurance cover
  - Details of relevant experience and references

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

6. NOTES

  - The contractor will liaise with the client's nominated
    representative to agree a suitable maintenance schedule.
  - Works may be adjusted seasonally to reflect the grounds'
    requirements, within the agreed annual hours.
  - Any additional works requested outside of this scope will
    be agreed and confirmed in writing prior to commencement.
  - The client reserves the right not to accept the lowest or
    any tender received.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Please submit all tender responses to the Estates / Facilities
team at Dame Hannah Rogers Trust.

